<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Panel grid rows, medium tier: 520dp to 639dp of available height — short and older
    phones. See values/integers.xml for what these are and why they are bucketed.

    Both counts are 1 here, same as the compact tier. Multiple rows start at h640dp.
    The two resources arrive at 1 for different reasons, so they are justified separately:

    panel_preset_grid_rows — readability. The preset adapters size a tile as
        (recycler height - rows * 6dp) / rows
    and make it square, so the row count divides the tile directly. Measured on a
    Pixel 10 Pro XL at 1344px wide:

        h640dp (997dp)   3 rows   215px tile     Styles grid
        h520dp (600dp)   2 rows   130px tile     <- was here
        values  (500dp)  1 row    189px tile

    The "eye" preview badge is a fixed 66px, so on the 130px tile it covered 51% of it,
    and on the 3D presets grid (106px tile) 62% — the badge read as the tile and the
    styles were impossible to tell apart. Note the absurdity the middle row created: the
    *shorter* 500dp screen showed a *larger* tile than the 600dp one. At 1 row this tier
    gets a 278px tile, the largest of the three, which is right — the strip has 99dp of
    height to spend and one style is worth showing properly.

    panel_color_grid_rows — height budget, not readability. A swatch is a hardcoded 26dp
    in layout_color_item.xml and the palette RecyclerViews are wrap_content, so the
    swatch measures exactly 78px in every tier no matter what this is set to; the row
    count only multiplies the strip's height by 32dp a row. The defect it caused here is
    the one values/integers.xml already documents for the compact tier: at 2 rows the
    palette ate the whole panel and Stroke's "Border width" slider sat entirely below the
    bottom edge, unreachable. One row gives that 32dp back and the slider returns. At
    h640dp four rows still leave the slider on screen, so that tier is left alone.
-->
<resources>
    <integer name="panel_color_grid_rows">1</integer>
    <integer name="panel_preset_grid_rows">1</integer>
</resources>
